! The held "a(n)": the determiner is chosen by the noun, which arrives after the
! rest of the clause is already shown. Until then it is "a", because the tail
! waiting for the noun is not the text the choice reads.
!
! Not in `hole.strokes`, because `scripts/check-hold.py` replays that through
! Plover and Plover gets this wrong: its `{=…}` reads the next action, and the
! tail's preview is that action, so the noun never reaches it ("a egg adds").
!buffer
#TPW-B
KAT
!buffer
#TPW-B
EG
!buffer
#TPWE-B
EG
!buffer
#+TPW-B
EG

! With nothing after the hole there is no tail, so the noun is the next text.
!buffer
#+TPW
EG
